<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:bioc="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn/biocolor/1.0" xmlns:color="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/non-normative/color/1.0" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_1nfyr6w" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="bpmn-js (https://demo.bpmn.io)" exporterVersion="18.13.2">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_0uirzwp">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_1ktecoe" name="ECC Solar" processRef="Process_0uc5le0" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0rki01r">
      <bpmn:text>Here's the uber chart! It will get changed and updated a few more times before we're done.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1f7c26o">
      <bpmn:text>For some reason, the editor isn't letting me connect the data object to the data store, but naturally the idea is that the information we collect in the individual data objects will be stored so it can be recalled later in the process.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_10zdftj">
      <bpmn:text>Website or Sales Rep, doesn't matter, this gets generated and stored in Solbiz</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1kkq3xs">
      <bpmn:text>I understand that these are the steps that gives us the most information about what we'll practically need for a given job.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_048kc62">
      <bpmn:text>Name, Email, Home Address, Billing Address, Phone Number, Referral Status</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_15450vi">
      <bpmn:text>General Location, Job Type, Install Site, Sales Rep, Lead Installer, Warranty Type, Utility Company, Tax Credits, Financing Option, KMZ file</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_02nzpk0">
      <bpmn:text>Components, Electrical Materials, Etc.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1rln1zv">
      <bpmn:text>Travel, Labor, Inspection Status, Permits, Releases, Pictures</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1hcfw40">
      <bpmn:text>I know we're not supposed to have a lane for the system back-end, but I thought it would clarify what was being tracked where. A note about these data objects: much of this information will be scattered across many files. Understand that these objects may in fact represent folders of files in Google Docs and not one, standalone, file. Some of them may also nest in ways that isn't represented here such as how the Job Documentation object will likely just be a subfolder in the Google Drive which is represented by the Job Profile data object.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0xkuhrj">
      <bpmn:text>Original Wiring, Grounding Locations, Hazards, Marketing Photos, Meter Locations, Meter Boxes, Main Load Centers, Roof/Ground Location, Outstanding/Unforeseen Details</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0ey44z0">
      <bpmn:text>Doc Tube, Marketing Photos, Open Load Centers, Close-up of Meter Can, CID Inspection Stickers, Entire System Across Locations, Ground Work, Outstanding Details</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0z03kj6">
      <bpmn:text>I know we're not supposed to make lanes for anything outside the company structure with BPMN, but this is just for clarification.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:group id="Group_0tohapf" categoryValueRef="CategoryValue_0riwi2n" />
    <bpmn:group id="Group_0g8ze7l" categoryValueRef="CategoryValue_0z9nevc" />
    <bpmn:group id="Group_1s4vevf" categoryValueRef="CategoryValue_1syiywh" />
